# Keep docs in sync

A code change is not finished until `docs/` matches the code. Follow `.cursor/skills/plan-docs/SKILL.md`.

In the same turn as the code (not a follow-up), patch the files that apply:

| If you change | Also update |
|---------------|-------------|
| `server/app/router/**`, pydantic models | `docs/api.md` and the matching `docs/features/*.md` |
| `server/app/db_models/**`, `server/alembic/**` | `docs/data-model.md` |
| `docker-compose*.yml`, `nginx/**`, `Dockerfile*`, `.env.example`, `wait-for-db.sh` | `docs/architecture.md`, `docs/operations.md` |
| `console/src/**` | the matching `docs/features/*.md` |

Add, rename, or delete `docs/features/<name>.md` when a user-facing capability is added or removed. Keep `docs/README.md` links in sync.

```
# ❌ BAD — ship the route only
@router.get("/foo")

# ✅ GOOD — same turn
@router.get("/foo")  +  document GET /api/.../foo in docs/api.md
```

Skip only a pure refactor with no behavior, API, schema, UI, or ops change. Say so explicitly.
